.TH PONS 1 "2026-10-23" "pons 0.1.0" "Pons Asinorum"
.SH NAME
pons \- falsifier-first static analyzer with explicit evidence tiers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pons
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B pons scan
.I PATH
.RB [ --format
.IR human | json | sarif ]
.RB [ --fail-on
.IR info | warn | error ]
.RB [ --config
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ --rule
.IR ID ]
.RB [ --lang
.IR python | javascript | typescript | tsx | rust ]
.RB [ --no-speculative ]
.RB [ --explain ]
.RB [ --fail-on-skips ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Pons scans source without executing project code. Findings carry a tier and an
evidence class derived from that tier.
.B SPECULATIVE
findings are demoted in every output format and never satisfy a
.B --fail-on
threshold. A skipped file or subtree is reported on stderr, in JSON
.BR scanned.skipped ,
and in SARIF invocation notifications; it is not silently treated as a pass.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B scan
Scan a file or directory. Optional flags:
.BR --format ,
.BR --fail-on ,
.BR --config ,
.BR --rule ,
.BR --lang ,
.BR --no-speculative ,
.BR --explain ,
.BR --fail-on-skips .
.TP
.B catalogue
Print the rule catalogue generated from the live registry.
.TP
.B man
Generate a man page from the same clap command model as
.BR --help .
.TP
.B doctor
Report optional adapter executables on
.BR PATH ;
do not claim they are tested.
.TP
.B trace
Check an explicitly supplied ordered JSON trace against a TOML protocol:
.B pons trace EVENTS.json --protocol PROTOCOL.toml .
No source-code event inference is performed.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Scan or command completed below the selected threshold.
.TP
.B 1
A non-speculative finding reached
.B --fail-on
or a trace contained protocol violations.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid input, configuration/protocol error, unopenable scan root, or
.B --fail-on-skips
with at least one skipped path.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B pons.toml
at the scan root, or
.BR --config ,
accepts
.B [identity]
and
.B [suppress]
with
.BR rules ,
.BR paths ,
and
.BR [[suppress.allow]] .
Unknown keys and unknown suppressed rule IDs fail. Inline source suppressions
use a real comment containing
.BR "pons:allow <rule-id>" .
.SH PLANNED COMMANDS
The following are planned and are not accepted by this binary:
.BR "pons challenge" ,
.BR "pons extract" ,
.BR "pons spell" ,
.BR "pons search" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR docs/USAGE.adoc ,
